🧠 **Real-World Analogy:**
If nodes are individual train cars, then the LinkedList class is like the 
train conductor who:
- Knows where the train starts (head pointer)
- Can add new cars to the train
- Can remove cars from the train
- Can tell you information about the entire train

💻 **Mini Example 2: Basic LinkedList Class**
```java
public class LinkedList {
    private Node head;  // Points to first node (start of chain)
    
    // Constructor - creates empty list
    public LinkedList() {
        this.head = null;
    }
    
    // Check if list is empty
    public boolean isEmpty() {
        return head == null;
    }
    
    // Display all elements
    public void display() {
        if (head == null) {
            System.out.println("List is empty");
            return;
        }
        
        Node current = head;
        System.out.print("List: ");
        while (current != null) {
            System.out.print(current.data + " -> ");
            current = current.next;
        }
        System.out.println("null");
    }
    
    // Get size of list
    public int size() {
        int count = 0;
        Node current = head;
        while (current != null) {
            count++;
            current = current.next;
        }
        return count;
    }
}
```

